The trigger picker showed and removed trigger.custom entries but offered
no way to add one, and screenpipe stores them without evaluating them.

- "Dès que…" entry, first group of "Add trigger": a natural-language
  condition saved into trigger.custom through persistTrigger; once the
  config is saved, POST http://127.0.0.1:4300/api/pipes/synchroniser
  (fire-and-forget, errors ignored). Empty text is refused.
- Under the custom chips: the engine state for this pipe, polled every
  3 s from GET /api/pipes/etat while at least one custom chip is shown
  (branchée, à valider, non branchée, erreur, en attente de traduction,
  moteur injoignable), with Valider / Refuser buttons that call
  /api/actions/<id>/valider|refuser, then refresh.
- Text-only rendering, no URL other than 127.0.0.1:4300, no key.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
